data={'answer': 'Salesforce provides official Hosted MCP Servers that allow AI agents to securely interact with Salesforce data and logic using the Model Context Protocol [1][2]. These servers eliminate the need for custom middleware by providing a governed, OAuth-authenticated endpoint directly from your Salesforce org [1][3].

To connect an MCP-compatible client, you configure the server in your Salesforce org and provide the client with the endpoint URL [1][3]. A minimal configuration example for a client like Claude Desktop looks like this:

```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "salesforce-org": {
      "url": "https://<your-org>.my.salesforce.com/services/mcp/v1/<server-name>",
      "transport": "http",
      "headers": {
        "Authorization": "Bearer <access_token>"
      }
    }
  }
}
```

Administrators can also create custom MCP servers to combine tools or expose Apex, Flows, and API endpoints [4][5]. Configuration is managed within Salesforce Setup under Integration, Salesforce MCP Servers [4][5].', 'citations': [{'author': 'Salesforce', 'id': 'https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/hosted-mcp-servers/guide/hosted-mcp-servers-overview.html', 'title': 'Get Started | Hosted MCP Servers | Salesforce Developers', 'url': 'https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/hosted-mcp-servers/guide/hosted-mcp-servers-overview.html'}, {'author': 'Salesforce', 'favicon': 'https://developer.salesforce.com/ns-assets/favicon.ico', 'id': 'https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/ai/agentforce/guide/mcp.html', 'image': 'https://a.sfdcstatic.com/shared/images/c360-nav/icons.svg#hamburger-blue', 'title': 'MCP Solutions | Headless Agentforce Development | Agentforce Developer Guide | Salesforce Developers', 'url': 'https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/ai/agentforce/guide/mcp.html'}, {'id': 'https://github.com/SalesforceDiariesBySanket/Salesforce-Hosted-Custom-Mcp-Server', 'title': 'SalesforceDiariesBySanket/Salesforce-Hosted-Custom-Mcp-Server', 'url': 'https://github.com/SalesforceDiariesBySanket/Salesforce-Hosted-Custom-Mcp-Server'}, {'author': 'Salesforce', 'favicon': 'https://developer.salesforce.com/ns-assets/favicon.ico', 'id': 'https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/hosted-mcp-servers/guide/custom-servers.html', 'image': 'https://a.sfdcstatic.com/shared/images/c360-nav/icons.svg#hamburger-blue', 'title': 'Build Custom MCP Servers | Hosted MCP Servers | Salesforce Developers', 'url': 'https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/hosted-mcp-servers/guide/custom-servers.html'}, {'author': 'Salesforce', 'favicon': 'https://developer.salesforce.com/ns-assets/favicon.ico', 'id': 'https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/hosted-mcp-servers/references/reference/custom-servers.html', 'image': 'https://a.sfdcstatic.com/shared/images/c360-nav/icons.svg