data={'answer': 'There is no single official Telegram MCP server; rather, several independent implementations exist that connect AI assistants to your personal Telegram account via the MTProto protocol [1][2][3][4]. These servers function as userbots, providing full access to your chats, media, and history without the limitations of the official Telegram Bot API [1][5][6].

Popular implementations include:

- mcp-telegram: A widely used TypeScript-based server using GramJS [1][6].
- eraga/telegram-mcp: Features a background SQLite archival system [2].
- Baho73/mcp-telegram: Supports a shared-daemon mode for concurrent multi-agent access [4].

To configure these with an MCP client like Claude Desktop, you typically add the server to your configuration file [2]:

```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "telegram": {
      "command": "npx",
      "args": ["-y", "mcp-telegram"]
    }
  }
}
```

You will need to provide your Telegram API credentials from my.telegram.org [7][3].', 'citations': [{'id': 'https://github.com/mcp-telegram/mcp-telegram/', 'title': 'mcp-telegram/mcp-telegram', 'url': 'https://github.com/mcp-telegram/mcp-telegram/'}, {'id': 'https://github.com/eraga/telegram-mcp', 'publishedDate': '2026-01-11T00:00:00.000Z', 'title': 'eraga/telegram-mcp', 'url': 'https://github.com/eraga/telegram-mcp'}, {'id': 'https://www.npmjs.com/package/mcp-telegram', 'title': 'mcp-telegram', 'url': 'https://www.npmjs.com/package/mcp-telegram'}, {'id': 'https://github.com/Baho73/mcp-telegram', 'title': 'Baho73/mcp-telegram', 'url': 'https://github.com/Baho73/mcp-telegram'}, {'id': 'https://github.com/AlexeyPevz/telegram-mcp', 'title': 'AlexeyPevz/telegram-mcp', 'url': 'https://github.com/AlexeyPevz/telegram-mcp'}, {'id': 'https://www.npmjs.com/package/@overpod/mcp-telegram', 'title': '@overpod/mcp-telegram', 'url': 'https://www.npmjs.com/package/@overpod/mcp-telegram'}, {'id': 'https://github.com/chigwell/telegram-mcp', 'publishedDate': '2025-03-20T14:06:35.000Z', 'title': 'chigwell/telegram-mcp', 'url': 'https://github.com/chigwell/telegram-mcp'}, {'id': 'https://github.com/chaindead/telegram-mcp', 'publishedDate': '2025-04-01T14:43:04.000Z', 'title': 'chaindead/telegram-mcp', 'url': 'https://github.com/chaindead/telegram-mcp'}]} error=None log_id='log_BkghZv03z9mx'

data={'answer': 'There is no single official WhatsApp-branded MCP server; rather, several independent developers have created production-ready MCP servers that interface with the official Meta WhatsApp Business Cloud API [1][2][3][4]. These servers allow AI clients like Claude or Cursor to send messages, manage templates, and handle business profile data [1][2][5].

To use one, you typically configure your MCP client (such as Claude Desktop) with the server's command and your Meta API credentials [2][3][4][6].

Example configuration for Claude Desktop using `npx`:

```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "whatsapp-business": {
      "command": "npx",
      "args": ["-y", "whatsapp-business-mcp-server"],
      "env": {
        "WHATSAPP_TOKEN": "your_access_token",
        "WHATSAPP_PHONE_NUMBER_ID": "your_phone_id"
      }
    }
  }
}
```

Key repositories include:
- Gonzalez8/whatsapp-business-mcp [4][7]
- FredShred7/whatsapp-mcp-server [3]
- saravanaspar/WBMCP [1]
- tkhattar14/whatsapp-business-mcp [2]
- spirit122/whatsapp-mcp-server (Cloudflare-hosted) [8]

Ensure you have a Meta Developer account and a configured WhatsApp Business App to obtain the required Access Token and Phone Number ID [3][6][5].', 'citations': [{'id': 'https://github.com/saravanaspar/WBMCP', 'publishedDate': '2026-06-04T13:28:32.000Z', 'title': 'saravanaspar/WBMCP', 'url': 'https://github.com/saravanaspar/WBMCP'}, {'id': 'https://github.com/tkhattar14/whatsapp-business-mcp', 'publishedDate': '2026-03-28T13:11:08.000Z', 'title': 'tkhattar14/whatsapp-business-mcp', 'url': 'https://github.com/tkhattar14/whatsapp-business-mcp'}, {'id': 'https://github.com/fredshred7/whatsapp-mcp-server', 'title': 'FredShred7/whatsapp-mcp-server', 'url': 'https://github.com/fredshred7/whatsapp-mcp-server'}, {'id': 'https://github.com/Gonzalez8/whatsapp-business-mcp', 'publishedDate': '2026-04-08T09:29:50.000Z', 'title': 'Gonzalez8/whatsapp-business-mcp', 'url': 'https://github.com/Gonzalez8/whatsapp-business-mcp'}, {'id': 'https://github.com/networkerman/whatsapp-cloud-api-mcp-server', 'title': 'networkerman/whatsapp-cloud-api-mcp-server', 'url': 'https://github.com/networkerman/whatsapp-cloud-api-mcp-server'}, {'id': 'https://github.com/rukman7/whatsapp-mcp-server', 'publishedDate': '2026-03-28T00:00:00.000Z', 'title': 'rukman7/whatsapp-mcp-server', 'url': 'https://github.com/rukman7/whatsapp-mcp-server'}, {'id': 'https://registry.npmjs.org/whatsapp-business-mcp-server/-/whatsapp-business-mcp-server-1.1.0.tgz', 'title': 'whatsapp-business-mcp-server', 'url': 'https://registry.npmjs.org/whatsapp-business-mcp-server/-/whatsapp-business-mcp-server-1.1.0.tgz'}, {'id': 'https://github.com/spirit122/whatsapp-mcp-server', 'title': 'spirit122/whatsapp-mcp-server', 'url': 'https://github.com/spirit122/whatsapp-mcp-server'}]} error=None log_id='log_PhbR5-12QkdN'

data={'answer': 'Vonage provides two official Model Context Protocol (MCP) servers to integrate their platform with AI assistants and IDEs [1].

The Documentation MCP Server allows AI models to query official Vonage API documentation for guides and code snippets [1][2]. It is configured via an HTTP URL [3][4]:

```json
{
  "servers": {
    "vonage-docs": {
      "url": "https://documentation-mcp.vonage.dev/mcp",
      "type": "http"
    }
  }
}
```

The Server API Bindings MCP Server (or Tooling Server) enables AI agents to perform programmatic actions like managing applications, numbers, and reports [1][5]. It runs locally via stdio using the `@vonage/vonage-mcp-server-api-bindings` package [6][5]:

```json
{
  "servers": {
    "vonage-tooling": {
      "type": "stdio",
      "command": "npx",
      "args": ["-y", "@vonage/vonage-mcp-server-api-bindings"],
      "env": {
        "VONAGE_API_KEY": "YOUR_KEY",
        "VONAGE_API_SECRET": "YOUR_SECRET"
      }
    }
  }
}
```

