data={'answer': 'BigCommerce provides an official Storefront MCP server that allows AI agents to interact with a live storefront to search products, manage carts, and initiate checkouts [1][2]. To enable it, store owners must navigate to Settings, then Early Access in the BigCommerce control panel [1][2]. Once enabled, you receive a unique MCP server URL to configure in your AI client [1].

To add the server to your configuration, use the following command structure [1]:

```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "bigcommerce": {
      "command": "npx",
      "args": ["mcp-remote", "<YOUR_MCP_SERVER_URL>"]
    }
  }
}
```

Additionally, BigCommerce offers a separate official MCP server for developer documentation, which allows AI agents to reference API details and best practices [3]. You can connect this documentation server by adding the URL https://docs.bigcommerce.com/_mcp/server to your MCP configuration [3].', 'citations': [{'favicon': 'https://docs.bigcommerce.com/api/fern-docs/favicon.ico', 'id': 'https://docs.bigcommerce.com/developer/api-reference/mcp/overview', 'image': 'https://docs.bigcommerce.com/api/fern-docs/og?slug=developer%2Fapi-reference%2Fmcp%2Foverview', 'title': 'MCP Server Overview | BigCommerce Docs', 'url': 'https://docs.bigcommerce.com/developer/api-reference/mcp/overview'}, {'id': 'https://www.bigcommerce.com/blog/storefront-mcp/', 'image': 'https://storage.googleapis.com/s.mkswft.com/RmlsZTo4ZmJiYTYzMy1jOGUwLTQ4ZWEtOTRiNy1iZmUyZjRkYWIwMDU=/BigCommerce-Social-Image-Generic-Facebook.jpg', 'publishedDate': '2026-05-11T00:00:00.000Z', 'title': 'Build AI Shopping Agents with BigCommerce Storefront MCP', 'url': 'https://www.bigcommerce.com/blog/storefront-mcp/'}, {'id': 'https://docs.bigcommerce.com/developer/docs/ai-agent-setup', 'image': 'https://docs.bigcommerce.com/api/fern-docs/og?slug=developer%2Fdocs%2Fai-agent-setup', 'title': 'AI Agent Setup | BigCommerce Docs', 'url': 'https://docs.bigcommerce.com/developer/docs/ai-agent-setup'}, {'id': 'https://docs.bigcommerce.com/developer/api-reference/mcp/storefront/b2c', 'image': 'https://docs.bigcommerce.com/api/fern-docs/og?slug=developer%2Fapi-reference%2Fmcp%2Fstorefront%2Fb2c', 'title': 'B2C Storefront | BigCommerce Docs', 'url': 'https://docs.bigcommerce.com/developer/api-reference/mcp/storefront/b2c'}, {'id': 'https://www.bigcommerce.com/blog/model-context-protocol/', 'image': 'https://storage.googleapis.com/s.mkswft.com/RmlsZTo4ZmJiYTYzMy1jOGUwLTQ4ZWEtOTRiNy1iZmUyZjRkYWIwMDU=/BigCommerce-Social-Image-Generic-Facebook.jpg', 'publishedDate': '2025-09-18T05:00:00.000Z', 'title': 'Model Context Protocol (MCP): The New Standard Every AI Developer Should Know | BigCommerce', 'url': 'https://www.bigcommerce.com/blog/model-context-protocol/'}, {'favicon': 'https://docs.bigcommerce.com/api/fern-docs/favicon.ico', 'id': 'https://docs.bigcommerce.com/developer/api-reference/mcp/tool-resynchronization', 'image': 'https://docs.bigcommerce.com/api/fern-docs/og?slug=developer%2Fapi-reference%2Fmcp%2Ftool-resynchronization', 'title': 'Agent Behavior for Tool Resynchronization | BigCommerce Docs', 'url': 'https://docs.bigcommerce.com/developer/api-reference/mcp/tool-resynchronization'}, {'id': 'https://github.com/ackm04/bigcommerce-mcp', 'publishedDate': '2026-03-16T10:31:41.000Z', 'title': 'ackm04/bigcommerce-mcp', 'url': 'https://github.com/ackm04/bigcommerce-mcp'}, {'id': 'https://github.com/CDataSoftware/bigcommerce-mcp-server-by-cdata', 'publishedDate': '2025-06-23T19:36:59.000Z', 'title': 'CDataSoftware/bigcommerce-mcp-server-by-cdata', 'url': 'https://github.com/CDataSoftware/bigcommerce-mcp-server-by-cdata'}]} error=None log_id='log_8uM6hJC27ek4'

data={'answer': 'Squarespace provides an official, first-party MCP server at https://mcp.squarespace.com/mcp [1][2]. This server is designed for customer acquisition, specifically exposing tools for domain searching and business name generation [2]. It does not provide access to Squarespace Commerce APIs [2].

To use it, add the URL to your MCP client's configuration [2]. For stdio-only clients, you can bridge it using `mcp-remote` [2]:

```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "squarespace": {
      "command": "npx",
      "args": ["-y", "mcp-remote", "https://mcp.squarespace.com/mcp"]
    }
  }
}
```

