data={'answer': 'The Bright Data MCP server is an official tool that enables LLMs and AI agents to access, search, and extract real-time web data while bypassing anti-bot protections [1][2][3]. It supports both a fully managed remote instance and a self-hosted local instance [4][3].

To use the remote server, add the following URL to your MCP-compatible client (e.g., Claude Desktop, Cursor) using your API token [1][5]:

`https://mcp.brightdata.com/mcp?token=YOUR_API_TOKEN`

For local hosting, use the following configuration [1][2]:

```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "Bright Data": {
      "command": "npx",
      "args": ["@brightdata/mcp"],
      "env": {
        "API_TOKEN": "<your-api-token-here>"
      }
    }
  }
}
```

New accounts receive 5,000 free requests per month [1][4][6].', 'citations': [{'id': 'https://github.com/brightdata/brightdata-mcp/', 'title': 'brightdata/brightdata-mcp', 'url': 'https://github.com/brightdata/brightdata-mcp/'}, {'id': 'https://github.com/brightdata/brightdata-mcp/blob/0e9cbd3a658a8d61aa73f193ca17b8a7e945ee48/README.md', 'title': 'README.md', 'url': 'https://github.com/brightdata/brightdata-mcp/blob/0e9cbd3a658a8d61aa73f193ca17b8a7e945ee48/README.md'}, {'id': 'https://docs.brightdata.com/ai/mcp-server/faqs', 'title': 'Bright Data MCP FAQs', 'url': 'https://docs.brightdata.com/ai/mcp-server/faqs'}, {'id': 'https://docs.brightdata.com/products/mcp-server/overview', 'image': 'https://brightdata.mintlify.app/mintlify-assets/_next/image?url=%2F_mintlify%2Fapi%2Fog%3Fdivision%3DBright%2BData%2BMCP%26title%3DMCP%2Bserver%2Boverview%26description%3DUse%2Bthe%2BBright%2BData%2BMCP%2Bserver%2Bto%2Bgive%2BAI%2Bagents%2Breal-time%2Baccess%2Bto%2Bpublic%2Bweb%2Bdata%2Bwith%2B5%252C000%2Bfree%2Brequests%2Bper%2Bmonth%2Band%2Bzero%2Binfrastructure%2Bsetup.%26theme%3Da8eee9c6f82a74bc48a1ce82&w=1200&q=100', 'title': 'MCP server overview - Bright Data Docs', 'url': 'https://docs.brightdata.com/products/mcp-server/overview'}, {'id': 'https://docs.brightdata.com/ai/mcp-server/remote/quickstart', 'title': 'How to get started with remote MCP server', 'url': 'https://docs.brightdata.com/ai/mcp-server/remote/quickstart'}, {'id': 'https://brightdata.com/pricing/mcp-server', 'title': 'MCP Server Pricing', 'url': 'https://brightdata.com/pricing/mcp-server'}, {'id': 'https://brightdata.com/ai/mcp-server', 'title': '', 'url': 'https://brightdata.com/ai/mcp-server'}, {'id': 'https://docs.brightdata.com/ai/mcp-server/tools', 'title': '', 'url': 'https://docs.brightdata.com/ai/mcp-server/tools'}]} error=None log_id='log_AP0RhBWJAwy-'

data={'answer': 'The official Netlify MCP server is a tool that enables AI agents to interact directly with the Netlify platform, allowing them to create projects, trigger deployments, and manage infrastructure using natural language [1][2][3].

To use the official server, add the following configuration to your MCP client's configuration file [1][4]:

```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "netlify": {
      "command": "npx",
      "args": [
        "-y",
        "@netlify/mcp"
      ]
    }
  }
}
```

