data={'answer': 'Monday.com provides two primary ways to use the Model Context Protocol (MCP) to connect AI agents to their platform [1].

The hosted Platform MCP server is the recommended, zero-setup option for managing boards, items, and workflows [2][3]. You can configure it in your MCP client using the following URL [2]:

```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "monday-mcp": {
      "url": "https://mcp.monday.com/mcp"
    }
  }
}
```

Alternatively, you can run the local `@mondaydotcomorg/monday-api-mcp` server via `npx` for more control, such as customizing the source code or using the Apps Framework tools [3][4]. To use the local server, provide your API token via the `-t` flag or `MONDAY_TOKEN` environment variable [5][4]. For example, to enable the Apps Framework tools, use the following configuration [6]:

```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "monday-apps-mcp": {
      "command": "npx",
      "args": ["@mondaydotcomorg/monday-api-mcp@latest", "-t", "your_token", "-m", "apps"]
    }
  }
}
```', 'citations': [{'id': 'https://developer.monday.com/apps/docs/mcp-servers', 'title': 'MCP servers', 'url': 'https://developer.monday.com/apps/docs/mcp-servers'}, {'id': 'https://developer.monday.com/api-reference/docs/mondaycom-mcp', 'title': '', 'url': 'https://developer.monday.com/api-reference/docs/mondaycom-mcp'}, {'id': 'https://github.com/mondaycom/monday-ai', 'title': 'mondaycom/mcp', 'url': 'https://github.com/mondaycom/monday-ai'}, {'id': 'https://github.com/mondaycom/mcp/blob/master/README.md', 'title': 'README.md', 'url': 'https://github.com/mondaycom/mcp/blob/master/README.md'}, {'id': 'https://github.com/mondaycom/mcp/blob/master/packages/monday-api-mcp/README.md', 'title': 'packages/monday-api-mcp/README.md', 'url': 'https://github.com/mondaycom/mcp/blob/master/packages/monday-api-mcp/README.md'}, {'id': 'https://developer.monday.com/apps/docs/monday-apps-mcp', 'title': '', 'url': 'https://developer.monday.com/apps/docs/monday-apps-mcp'}, {'id': 'https://developer.monday.com/api-reference/docs/platform-mcp-tools', 'title': '', 'url': 'https://developer.monday.com/api-reference/docs/platform-mcp-tools'}, {'id': 'https://registry.npmjs.org/%40mondaydotcomorg%2Fmonday-api-mcp', 'publishedDate': '2025-04-03T00:00:00.000Z', 'title': '@mondaydotcomorg/monday-api-mcp', 'url': 'https://registry.npmjs.org/%40mondaydotcomorg%2Fmonday-api-mcp'}]} error=None log_id='log_1w9HT6Kfem3V'

data={'answer': 'ClickUp provides an official Model Context Protocol (MCP) server accessible via the URL https://mcp.clickup.com/mcp [1]. This server is hosted by ClickUp, uses OAuth for authentication, and is designed for multi-user environments [2].

To configure it, add the server to your MCP client's configuration file using the following command or JSON structure [1]:

```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "clickup": {
      "command": "npx",
      "args": ["-y", "mcp-remote", "https://mcp.clickup.com/mcp"]
    }
  }
}
```

For specific clients like Claude Desktop, you can also use the command `claude mcp add --transport http clickup https://mcp.clickup.com/mcp` [1]. Note that several third-party, community-maintained MCP servers for ClickUp also exist, which typically use personal API tokens and local execution instead of OAuth [2][3][4].', 'citations': [{'id': 'https://developer.clickup.com/docs/connect-an-ai-assistant-to-clickups-mcp-server-1', 'title': '', 'url': 'https://developer.clickup.com/docs/connect-an-ai-assistant-to-clickups-mcp-server-1'}, {'author': 'Nick Bester', 'favicon': 'https://clickup-cli.com/assets/clickup-cli-logo.svg', 'id': 'https://clickup-cli.com/mcp/', 'image': 'https://clickup-cli.com/assets/og-image.png', 'title': 'MCP Server | clickup-cli', 'url': 'https://clickup-cli.com/mcp/'}, {'id': 'https://www.npmjs.com/package/clickup-mcp-connector', 'title': 'clickup-mcp-connector', 'url': 'https://www.npmjs.com/package/clickup-mcp-connector'}, {'id': 'https://github.com/nazruden/clickup-mcp-server', 'title': 'Nazruden/clickup-mcp-server', 'url': 'https://github.com/nazruden/clickup-mcp-server'}, {'id': 'https://github.com/taazkareem/clickup-mcp-server/blob/main/docs/DOCUMENTATION.md', 'title': 'docs/DOCUMENTATION.md', 'url': 'https://github.com/taazkareem/clickup-mcp-server/blob/main/docs/DOCUMENTATION.md'}, {'id': 'https://github.com/taazkareem/clickup-mcp-server', 'publishedDate': '2025-12-24T00:00:00.000Z', 'title': 'taazkareem/clickup-mcp-server', 'url': 'https://github.com/taazkareem/clickup-mcp-server'}, {'id': 'https://github.com/cooperniebuhr/clickup-mcp-server', 'title': 'CooperNiebuhr/clickup-mcp-server', 'url': 'https://github.com/cooperniebuhr/clickup-mcp-server'}, {'id': 'https://github.com/Leanware-io/clickup-mcp-server', 'title': 'Leanware-io/clickup-mcp-server', 'url': 'https://github.com/Leanware-io/clickup-mcp-server'}]} error=None log_id='log_l9vUA5HVTYCX'

data={'answer': 'The Superhuman Docs API (formerly Coda) supports both API token and OAuth 2.0 authentication for developers building Packs [1][2][3].

For API tokens, use the CodaApiHeaderBearerToken authentication type, which provides a UI for users to generate tokens [4][5][6].

```javascript
pack.setUserAuthentication({
  type: sdk.AuthenticationType.CodaApiHeaderBearerToken,
  shouldAutoAuthSetup: true,
});
```

For OAuth 2.0, configure the authorization and token URLs provided by the API documentation [2][7].

```javascript
pack.setUserAuthentication({
  type: sdk.AuthenticationType.OAuth2,
  authorizationUrl: "https://example.com/authorize",
  tokenUrl: "https://api.example.com/token",
});
```

You must register your application in the provider's developer console to obtain a client ID and secret, which are entered in the Pack settings [2][7].', 'citations': [{'id': 'https://coda.io/apis/v1/openapi.yaml', 'title': 'openapi.yaml', 'url': 'https://coda.io/apis/v1/openapi.yaml'}, {'id': 'https://coda.io/packs/build/latest/guides/basics/authentication/oauth2/', 'image': 'https://docs.superhuman.com/packs/build/latest/assets/images/social/guides/basics/authentication/oauth2.png', 'title': 'Authenticating using OAuth - Superhuman Packs SDK', 'url': 'https://coda.io/packs/build/latest/guides/basics/authentication/oauth2/'}, {'id': 'https://coda.io/packs/build/latest/samples/topic/apis/', 'image': 'https://docs.superhuman.com/packs/build/latest/assets/images/social/samples/topic/apis.png', 'title': 'API setup samples - Superhuman Packs SDK', 'url': 'https://coda.io/packs/build/latest/samples/topic/apis/'}, {'favicon': 'https://coda.io/packs/build/latest/assets/favicon.svg', 'id': 'https://coda.io/packs/build/latest/reference/sdk/core/interfaces/CodaApiBearerTokenAuthentication/', 'image': 'https://coda.io/packs/build/latest/assets/images/social/reference/sdk/core/interfaces/CodaApiBearerTokenAuthentication.png', 'title': 'Interface: CodaApiBearerTokenAuthentication - Superhuman Packs SDK', 'url': 'https://coda.io/packs/build/latest/reference/sdk/core/interfaces/CodaApiBearerTokenAuthentication/'}, {'id': 'https://coda.github.io/packs-sdk/reference/sdk/enums/AuthenticationType/', 'image': 'https://cdn.coda.io/external/img/doc-banner-compressed-2x-v2.jpg', 'title': 'AuthenticationType - Coda Pack SDK', 'url': 'https://coda.github.io/packs-sdk/reference/sdk/enums/AuthenticationType/'}, {'id': 'https://coda.github.io/packs-sdk/reference/sdk/interfaces/CodaApiBearerTokenAuthentication/', 'image': 'https://cdn.coda.io/external/img/doc-banner-compressed-2x-v2.jpg', 'title': 'CodaApiBearerTokenAuthentication - Coda Pack SDK', 'url': 'https://coda.github.io/packs-sdk/refer