data={'answer': 'Coda provides an official, Coda-hosted Model Context Protocol (MCP) server that allows AI clients to read and write to your Coda documents [1][2]. It is currently in beta and requires no installation or self-hosting [2].

To connect, use the remote server URL: https://coda.io/apis/mcp [1][2].

For clients like Claude or Cursor, you can add this as a remote HTTP MCP server [2]. If using Claude Code, run:
```bash
claude mcp add --transport http Coda https://coda.io/apis/mcp
```
[2]

Alternatively, you can configure it manually in your client's MCP configuration file using a Personal Access Token [1]:
```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "Coda": {
      "url": "https://coda.io/apis/mcp",
      "headers": {
        "Authorization": "Bearer Your-Coda-Auth-Token"
      }
    }
  }
}
```
[1]

While several community-built MCP servers exist on GitHub for self-hosting, the official Coda-hosted server is the recommended option for most users [2].', 'citations': [{'id': 'https://help.coda.io/hc/en-us/articles/44722661982989-Connect-to-the-Coda-MCP', 'image': 'https://help.coda.io/hc/theming_assets/01JXX4E9YZC7DGQS631690PQST', 'title': 'Connect to the Coda MCP – Coda', 'url': 'https://help.coda.io/hc/en-us/articles/44722661982989-Connect-to-the-Coda-MCP'}, {'favicon': 'https://www.gamut.so/icon.svg?icon.0946_qax33tnk.svg?dpl=dpl_8GXRQxgPQhiF1rV5fs8i9qqpXf97', 'id': 'https://www.gamut.so/mcp/project-management/coda', 'image': 'https://www.gamut.so/opengraph-image', 'publishedDate': '2026-06-24T00:00:00.000Z', 'title': 'Coda MCP Server', 'url': 'https://www.gamut.so/mcp/project-management/coda'}, {'id': 'https://github.com/vish288/mcp-coda', 'title': 'vish288/mcp-coda', 'url': 'https://github.com/vish288/mcp-coda'}, {'favicon': 'https://help.superhuman.com/hc/theming_assets/01KQFVFPRQ52YFM4Q53HJC3FXP', 'id': 'https://help.superhuman.com/hc/en-us/articles/46210076980365-Connect-to-the-Coda-MCP', 'image': 'https://help.superhuman.com/hc/theming_assets/01KQFVFQ2P0DYZD404FX0YJ3E4', 'title': 'Connect to the Superhuman Docs MCP – Superhuman Help Center', 'url': 'https://help.superhuman.com/hc/en-us/articles/46210076980365-Connect-to-the-Coda-MCP'}, {'id': 'https://github.com/orellazri/coda-mcp', 'title': 'orellazri/coda-mcp', 'url': 'https://github.com/orellazri/coda-mcp'}, {'id': 'https://github.com/dustinrgood/coda-mcp', 'title': 'dustinrgood/coda-mcp', 'url': 'https://github.com/dustinrgood/coda-mcp'}, {'id': 'https://github.com/nkpar/coda-mcp', 'title': 'nkpar/coda-mcp', 'url': 'https://github.com/nkpar/coda-mcp'}, {'id': 'https://github.com/glorynguyen/coda-mcp/', 'title': 'glorynguyen/coda-mcp', 'url': 'https://github.com/glorynguyen/coda-mcp/'}]} error=None log_id='log_eEuNBo9_OBMc'

data={'answer': 'The Smartsheet MCP server is an open, protocol-based integration layer that allows any MCP-compliant AI client to interact with Smartsheet data using natural language [1]. It exposes Smartsheet's core work management objects—such as sheets, rows, columns, and workspaces—as tools that AI models can invoke to read, analyze, and manage data [2][1].

To connect, you must provide network access to the Smartsheet production environment for your region [3]:
- US: https://mcp.smartsheet.com
- EU: https://mcp.smartsheet.eu
- AU: https://mcp.smartsheet.au

Authentication is handled via OAuth 2.0 or personal access tokens [1]. You can configure the server in your AI client's settings or via CLI [4]. For example, in a configuration file:

```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "smartsheet-mcp": {
      "httpUrl": "https://mcp.smartsheet.com",
      "headers": {
        "Authorization": "Bearer ${SMARTSHEET_API_TOKEN}"
      }
    }
  }
}
```

