data={'answer': 'Otter.ai provides an official remote Model Context Protocol (MCP) server that allows AI assistants to access your meeting transcripts, summaries, and action items directly [1][2][3]. The server is hosted at https://mcp.otter.ai/mcp and uses OAuth for secure, user-authorized access [2][4].

To connect, add the endpoint to your MCP-compatible client (such as Claude, Cursor, or VS Code) [2][3]. For example, in Claude, you can typically use the following command [3]:

```bash
claude mcp add --transport http otter-ai https://mcp.otter.ai/mcp
```

Alternatively, you can configure it manually in your client's configuration file [4]:

```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "otter": {
      "type": "http",
      "url": "https://mcp.otter.ai/mcp"
    }
  }
}
```

